[{"id":"VRCE-6-77-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":1,"english":"Seeing the man and the Rākṣasa engaged in battle, with their whole soul, each eager to beat the other, like to elephants with the temporal juice trickling from their temples, desirous of beholding their encounter, Răvaņa's mighty and heroic brother, bearing an excellent bow, stood in front of the arena.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.738,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b702f080b4a08c4d01eae3040c39323e4b1cacdf0d5687532692c76835452556","compact":"12d0bdd5c3b59c5c5c23952664b9fb77b6c1ae610e14432be2c517f5938ee071","nasal":"12d0bdd5c3b59c5c5c23952664b9fb77b6c1ae610e14432be2c517f5938ee071"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":2,"english":"Taking up his post, he stretched his great bow and shot terrific sharp-pointed shafts at the Rāks asas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f58c3fa4964c7950f6c29ff15f864f525307e01d26ffe49139b8cf9fc5d75873","compact":"b611e7225bf4a4d073a2da4d2f9ab37469128f84844cde5ba378523bb7063524","nasal":"b611e7225bf4a4d073a2da4d2f9ab37469128f84844cde5ba378523bb7063524"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":3,"english":"Even like thunder-bolt cleaving mighty mountains, those shafts furnished with peacock's plumes falling powerfully (upon the foe), rent the Raksasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c53c555c75b63f0035c25868ab63ea0011141ec07e41c1e8bbd7fed5d4a26638","compact":"e232d43182171b4da93ce5c6e30e7ca5e2058c37c19065c17e2b263a00a5e9a4","nasal":"5f28156b6b4c709be5bfe91a6cb8a754e7598da9cd16f38268e9a8e960293cd5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":4,"english":"Those foremost of Raksasas, Vibhisana's followers, also in the encounter discharged darts and scimitars and pațțiśas at heroic Rākşasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.632,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3a76488f86cdcf8b76cb629af094fed3a5af48977ee11cb6334d054c99b3108f","compact":"fcd3946378d91c205373d7a9e32ab843bfedf4e300b5b53d33f826afb3375eb6","nasal":"fcd3946378d91c205373d7a9e32ab843bfedf4e300b5b53d33f826afb3375eb6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":5,"english":"Surrounded by those Raksasas, Vibhisana, then in the midst of his followers, appeared like an elephant in the midst of young ones.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7a152d03c0a8044482dffe5d629ff77899dc0eef14430f39c20bae44cfd762c4","compact":"c4d26fafe187c9eec09b80ec135d10f3d261d560d6d393a1a5bcb4870012f281","nasal":"c4d26fafe187c9eec09b80ec135d10f3d261d560d6d393a1a5bcb4870012f281"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":6,"english":"Then inciting the monkeys, whose dear object was to slay Ravana, that one versed in time, the foremost of Rākşasas,spoke seasonably thus.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.571,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fc6b5c2a558392586ebb7250beacabab7d3ef04523329e52ff83d59bd27246a2","compact":"2152c4f3b2965b702af07cbadac5ab697d200a9b8a0b04802a927a5662d318da","nasal":"2152c4f3b2965b702af07cbadac5ab697d200a9b8a0b04802a927a5662d318da"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":7,"english":"This one that stay (in the field) is the sole and mighty support of the Raksasa-chief; and this is his remaining force. Why then do the monkeychiefs remain inactive? On this wicked Rāksasa being slain on the edge of battle, the remnant of his army, with the single exception of Rāvawa, is destroyed.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"de58141ef10a551c71e82befb58cef09cdf934a76ee77995fd4e8bd9c5a7045e","compact":"439cec6b4b33aa794251c6d1de1bedaa827c848682a2191ed5397b1db55ea90e","nasal":"3f5dfd4344f331eced4814b95c4505697c115bc9d3c7f7f2e534c872f84de6bf"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":8,"english":"This one that stay (in the field) is the sole and mighty support of the Raksasa-chief; and this is his remaining force. Why then do the monkeychiefs remain inactive? On this wicked Rāksasa being slain on the edge of battle, the remnant of his army, with the single exception of Rāvawa, is destroyed.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.845,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e7ed20101dc61247c909da6e757c520f9283f8e7663fe8dcedd16dca54cf9d25","compact":"eee98c9b52b7672dff234f486d