8","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"90d036e40333f1e33144fe14f303ce648d5c775572fd30a83d62f2e74e781c1c","compact":"d6fdedda30fecd865ba45937aea4c808d5ebdc13e19ceb1561301a11617a9170","nasal":"ca44b61a41215703a0d114316c78cb51495b90b2f675ffc0aef4faae02a767fd"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":19,"english":"Thereat Räkşasas, endowed with exceeding strength, equipped with various weapons reproaching the lord of bears, as he was engaged in smiting (the foe), and renouncing fear, with shafts and sharp axes and pațțiśas and yaşțis, and tomaras, in the encounter assailed Jambavān, who was engaged in beating the Räkşasa forces.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.711,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b6cdc887284bb12c1fce98a5ce9fc6a7c2c452b4c7c1edfc2556b29effcf722e","compact":"3b7849974a48a28eb4353f2b4c3032c5b394ff17565a7be4c8b7848eea943610","nasal":"c656e0d366a5f59297cfdb26456ec815c4891bab28e12f3401e3f08369799967"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":20,"english":"That conflict between the monkeys and the Rākşasas, waxed furious, like to the tumultuous encounter of the immortals and the Asuras fired with wrath.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"047067e78a4c87a69fb4817d648ce1c1c15b2ef4f2555a15326d31fea34cfe9b","compact":"fc42e663c5a3327895a6275be5a0f5000eddf9d848787cf8cc7969c1fac4d6ce","nasal":"fc42e663c5a3327895a6275be5a0f5000eddf9d848787cf8cc7969c1fac4d6ce"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":21,"english":"The magnanimous Hanumān incapable of being approached growing wroth, uprooting a mountain, and putting down Lakşmaņa from his back, began a great carnage among the Rākşasas by thousands.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.516,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"618ad9a44c68fd559ff60cf2571546e0593fcf6fd1387b5a4ed4cb4c83fcf846","compact":"3731e2bdadca1195714d231154688fa5df812550510beb280a2e9118ce68d7ee","nasal":"3731e2bdadca1195714d231154688fa5df812550510beb280a2e9118ce68d7ee"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-22","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":22,"english":"And fighting a furious fight with his uncle, the powerful Indrajit, slayer of hostile heroesagain rushed against Lakşmaņa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.721,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077022","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"65329a56e25fbe1da7e608f58488b9ca4aa185c762fec199051b285bf0b42652","compact":"ce021926b08a95460f45f46fc73ef9354e36265664b6cf40efaaa5fb1b706a92","nasal":"0ab7b0c3401d7e88821618bdc9373e546632484279aa1733381bb91a72e40813"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-23","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":23,"english":"Then there took place an encounter between those heroes in the field, Laksmana and the Räksasa-discharging vollies of shafts and smiting each other; and those mighty and impetuous ones repeatedly covered each other with networks of arrows; like to the sun and the moon covered by clouds at the expiration of Summer.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077023","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"28a68da01b3ac5e64bfb3e33b29ffbef8d915fdf5cd5e63b10557fabc8592b0d","compact":"bb786fd965bd39abda7f6f7717f39e08088a98b83b5a726776780e995c9e09b3","nasal":"81cfd5791e7cf713dcb59a4cc65268dd8cd3ca364345f92b346b48c97691882c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-24","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":24,"english":"Then there took place an encounter between those heroes in the field, Laksmana and the Räksasa-discharging vollies of shafts and smiting each other; and those mighty and impetuous ones repeatedly covered each other with networks of arrows; like to the sun and the moon covered by clouds at the expiration of Summer.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077024","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fa6375a3404e0fb104428cb88437f6d6d3831c7aebc27ea1b3f860f780480ac6","compact":"ec63ec80b736b0a2423da8355bf3d3bf8927412d0242729198fa32a9dc6e1579","nasal":"94b9cd299881288439d0c8a00302c8495469c637b16c4777c269ee1d81220ef4"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-25","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":25,"english":"And on account of their light-handedness, neither discharge of arrows, nor the drawing of the bow; nor the setting of the shaft on the bowstring; not the taking of the bow; nor the selection of shafts; nor the clenching fast of their fists; nor the hitting of aims, could be perceived as they faught on.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077025","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"12b739d03a76a12e20633c6f941a9dbf6567f3206829bb3ddf031a19d4398bd6","compact":"4dee47658aad27dc69ab3b1e5be1cf9ddf5a7f7893446ad208b5b30de9f8a92c","nasal":"4dee47658aad27dc69ab3b1e5be1cf9ddf5a7f7893446ad208b5b30de9f8a92c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-26","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":26,"english":"And on account of their light-handedness, neither discharge of arrows, nor the drawing of the bow; nor the setting of the shaft on the bowstring; not the taking of the bow; nor the selection of shafts; nor the clenching fast of their fists; nor the hitting of aims, could be perceived as they faught on. In consequence of the sky being covered with networks of arrows all around, discharged powerfully from their bows, the forms (of objects) could not be discovered.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.453,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-21","DUTT-6-89-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077026","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"da9da39b84c4f14a3b886c2f4f7c6ae793d8d3bcf13ecd3ac06c639eafb89e0f","compact":"19eceec229dc70dc2074fb87edea306c1506aa1bafe9ce51cac5b3fcc8db86d8","nasal":"19eceec229dc70dc2074fb87edea306c1506aa1bafe9ce51cac5b3fcc8db86d8"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-27","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":27,"english":"In consequence of the sky being covered with networks of arrows all around, discharged powerfully from their bows, the forms (of objects) could not be discovered.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.483,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077027","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fef8d689722d24ad74eaee9a0d15070b806cdb3c5dbf3f56446bf4d524559af4","compact":"3c6bab5dd2133cac15e972b29e5fd621046bfa4b0d36c2b54a7c2aecc9da0d39","nasal":"e8a7b5d09cd273430bdc0870082b8d9f3d1d76546fc24e308f1cc15185ca8717"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-28","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":28,"english":"And all being overspread with gloom, a mighty fright took possession (of creatures) when the Sun having ascended the setting-hill, and darkness environing all objects. And that day* mighty torrents of blood flowed in thousands of streams; and fierce beasts of prey set up terrific yells (all around). And at that hour the wind did not blow, and fire did not blaze. * Aiya today in the text. The Maharsis said, 'Fair befell creatures.' And the Gandharvas along with the Cāranas grew exceedingly agitated.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.303,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-26","DUTT-6-89-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077028","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d5fc6f83b779b8b8fa47fab8d022936e23c13d2eacee27eec0f0f7a5bc79f3bf","compact":"86028fe37281a82e9e2dc11e5cf54d46cb2b05d609e45106ced207c996dc8efb","nasal":"be77f88f576e8448b157e400979cba904fa40412a1234cfdb5b59a105c670858"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-29","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":29,"english":"Then Sumitrā's son pierced the four black steeds of the leonine Räksasa, caparisoned in gold.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077029","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a611972091ac6d68825c4129a72617a4a64a6d6d0db2539d238ea5cca654d0db","compact":"3e04d3b85718d2c940401a0ed9067948b58daa84406b435a1edf2d8880c0fbea","nasal":"3e04d3b85718d2c940401a0ed9067948b58daa84406b435a1edf2d8880c0fbea"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-30","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":30,"english":"Then he hit at (Indrajit's) charioteer with another yellow and sharpened javelin splendid, furnished with feathers; and resembling the thunder-bolt of the great Indra. And through his fleet handedness the graceful son of Raghu with the thunder-bolt of his shaft, resonant with the sound of his palm, separated the (charioteer's head) from his trunk.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.596,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077030","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"87213dae90952129a5b3848c383b9aed1388b446015df9a5616a452b078bdaa5","compact":"955ef384644d5f1e95f3d309e068d5fedde5de1c6fe44b2ecaade6d7abdb98e3","nasal":"955ef384644d5f1e95f3d309e068d5fedde5de1c6fe44b2ecaade6d7abdb98e3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-31","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":31,"english":"Seeing his charioteer slain in the contest, Rāvana's son forewent his martial ardour, and was cast down.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.714,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077031","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"78c1c1ced718afdbf09dcf806248d0f1ae0d7249082d52b0bb7bfb5427431abc","compact":"86cb346356c48118c82f6b90c489bf2ce0391cf1bdd8f60789f87df5fd1c81cf","nasal":"3bd0f2eb7bf3818d5ae6aa2ea76236a0f862941a8caa8d6802f488264eeb1d5b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-32","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":32,"english":"Seeing the Rākşasa with his face fallen, the leaders of monkey-hands, were exceedingly delighted and rendered homage to Lakşmaņa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077032","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a92cf213771c50fe29cdbe5d835192e7acc96ba3d790a6a45e7f199cbb9aa063","compact":"c15e38f61bc057d884dce9635c5ec80135bddab0386df5c4a11866dabf08d6a0","nasal":"d853dc251cbde08ab2d3105fc24aaf886084f5eed836c9051b6d3af9aa0c2b09"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-33","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":33,"english":"Then those monkey-chiefs— Pramāthi, Rabhasa, Sarabha and Gandamādana, not brooking (their foe) summoned their impetuosity.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.6,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077033","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ed93d91d08e5b700af62d2954e946c99bb59cbf61bdc83953d96f9ccc38b58bd","compact":"0513bd1949baffc67d4950bdeeb805cbad41280b3af9721345cd8e68f5cfefd3","nasal":"9cf09f9a44b4bd059575447b899b085be1e77fac26fb49af534e047df7335a84"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-34","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":34,"english":"And suddenly springing up, those highly powerful monkeys endowed with terrific prowess descended upon those four best of steeds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077034","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6aae48d8a3b96162e476990691f21757b5e458dfe7e2fe53c6d2f0895cbd67fd","compact":"caf0aa1e16a09ba0b985258552fe12cb02d7bdc83101856668bf92671c1c83cc","nasal":"caf0aa1e16a09ba0b985258552fe12cb02d7bdc83101856668bf92671c1c83cc"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-35","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":35,"english":"On those chargers being assailed by those monkeys resembling mountains, blood gushed out of their mouths.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077035","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d74fa60c5d6b84548ce39abc3d39e5a6923f179e68f28e10feff0efca74dfaa2","compact":"d44490cd955e27c258986c22c231644e832cc5a5b8402b120350f4b9678038b9","nasal":"d44490cd955e27c258986c22c231644e832cc5a5b8402b120350f4b9678038b9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-36","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":36,"english":"Then the steeds were smashed and sent to the ground. And having slain the steeds, and smitten the mighty car-warrior,* again by a vehement bound, came to the side of Laksmana. *Maharatham (ac.) may also mean mighty car. By the way the samasa or junction called Tatpurusha is a frequent source of obscurity in Sanskrit specially where the gender of the word without samása is the same with that of the thing signified by the samāsa, as in this case.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077036","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e23ef4bcb310ed826d422dee3ded8186f941eb2d15b6d3500163fbee7e8792b8","compact":"eef9bc54d216713bf6e28e943c901d877f043aef1a548af7364f285fb51e605e","nasal":"716862fee234c85b7ee0b87807fee17ae00e32df95a5a150226e58d27d2d9038"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-37","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":37,"english":"Springing down from his car whose steeds had been slain, Ravana's son, his charioteer having been pounded, charged the son of Sumitra with arrows.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077037","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"91e0422b66f71966b11ef7dc223eedfbad8384383b21d93a80c7be0517aeaafc","compact":"136a2c3522380b980019385ff620d7a6852dfea4a5b78b25f342dbb68593b905","nasal":"136a2c3522380b980019385ff620d7a6852dfea4a5b78b25f342dbb68593b905"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-77-38","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":77,"verse":38,"english":"Then Lakşmaņa resembling the great Indra, on (Indrajit's) best of chargers having been despatched, in the encounter began to terribly rive with arrows discharged (his foe) footing on the earth and showering excellent sharpened shafts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.474,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-89-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6077038","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"14765b0750114d93318103fcbcd3a88940788a9b6e0ddaac9aa82ee561c215b1","compact":"6767d932bed458bfd30ecf697596bc785726588cc3e0f0c8b6b1e28dfeb00ffb","nasal":"9bdef57f2f49e61d4358f9d68f53278f21589072678d1ed5a96aacc42a190896"}}]
